# Footnotes: calls written in a Markdown, and a note whose content is a Markdown.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Footnotes · Notes in Markdown
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Section:
		Text: Footnotes
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Notes in Markdown
		Paragraph: Inside a `Markdown` the calls work without `Markup`. The note itself can be a `Markdown` whose first block is a paragraph, with bold, italic and links.
			Style: intro
		Markdown:
			Content >>
				The workshop uses walnut from the valley[^wood] and wool from a
				cooperative in the hills[^wool].
		Footnote:
			Id: wood
			Markdown:
				Content >>
					Dried for **two years** before it is cut.
		Footnote:
			Id: wool
			Markdown:
				Content >>
					See [the cooperative](https://stxt.dev) for its *certificates*.
